  "verbalization": "Quercetin Glucuronide appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a multi-step pathway. The first evidence links Quercetin Glucuronide to SN12K1, which is targeted by Penicinoline, and subsequently to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second evidence shows a direct interaction between Quercetin Glucuronide and Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is targeted by a compound that also interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Quercetin Glucuronide may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through different molecular pathways, potentially by influencing the activity of SN12K1 or Phosphodiesterase 6C. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex network of interactions that could underlie the observed effects, emphasizing the role of these targets in the broader biological context.",
